# Cryptography Visualizer & Multimedia Encryption System

A Python-based cryptography learning toolkit that demonstrates classical and modern encryption algorithms through step-by-step execution. The project focuses on internal working visualization rather than black-box encryption.

---

## Overview

This project implements multiple encryption techniques in a modular format to help understand how cryptographic systems transform data at each stage.

It supports both text-based and multimedia data processing, including image and audio streams.

The system is designed for academic learning and algorithm exploration.

---

## Implemented Modules

### 1. Plaintext Encryption & Decryption
- Character-level transformation logic
- Basic reversible encryption model

### 2. XOR Cipher
- Bitwise XOR-based symmetric encryption
- Demonstrates fundamental cryptographic operation

### 3. Image Encryption
- Pixel-level manipulation
- Array-based transformation of image data

### 4. Audio Encryption
- Byte-stream processing of audio files
- Demonstrates multimedia encryption pipeline

### 5. DES (Data Encryption Standard - Simplified Model)
- Block-based encryption structure
- Feistel-style round simulation

### 6. AES (Advanced Encryption Standard - Educational Model)
- 10-round encryption flow simulation
- Includes:
  - State matrix formation
  - SubBytes transformation (simplified)
  - ShiftRows operation
  - MixColumns (educational approximation)
  - AddRoundKey using XOR

### 7. RSA Cryptosystem
- Public key cryptography implementation
- Includes:
  - Prime number validation
  - Euler’s Totient Function (φ)
  - Key pair generation (public/private keys)
  - Encryption and decryption workflow

---

## Key Concepts Demonstrated

- Symmetric and asymmetric encryption
- Block cipher architecture
- Bitwise operations (XOR)
- Matrix-based transformations
- Modular arithmetic in cryptography
- Multi-round encryption systems
- Multimedia data encryption principles

---

## Tech Stack

- Python 3.x
- Standard libraries only
- File I/O operations
- Mathematical computations

